      "data": {
        "label": "Frame",
        "params": {
          "title": "C — Exercice 1 : Normalisation Min-Max et Z-score",
          "color_index": 4
        }
      },
      "width": 1860,
      "height": 530,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nC_inst",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": {
        "x": -90,
        "y": 900
      },
      "style": {
        "width": 540,
        "height": 430
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "id": "nC_inst",
        "params": {
          "text": "EXERCICE 1 — Normalisation\n\nImplémentez les deux normalisations :\n\n1. Min-Max (ramène entre 0 et 1)\n   x_norm = (x - min) / (max - min)\n\n2. Z-score (mean=0, std=1)\n   x_std = (x - mean) / std\n\nAppliquez sur TOUTES les colonnes\nnumériques (sauf 'target').\n\nRésultats :\nout_data   = df normalisé (Min-Max)\nout_scalar = écart-type moyen après norm.\n\nVérifiez que Min-Max donne bien [0,1] !",
          "bg_color": "#fef9c3",
          "text_color": "#713f12"
        }
      },
      "width": 540,
      "height": 430,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dsC",
      "type": "ml_sklearn_dataset",
      "position": {
        "x": 490,
        "y": 920
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Iris Ex1",
        "params": {
          "dataset": 0
        }
